      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 8,500 mg per dose, or 25,500 mg per day, is far above the maximum for metformin. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg per day, and most people take 500\u20131,000 mg per dose. A dose this size risks severe lactic acidosis. It looks like a typo.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg per day, the labeled maximum.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 1,500 mg per day, a common regimen.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg per day.\n\nTell me the dose you want, and confirm it with your supervising resident or attending if you're unsure. I'll enter it then. If 8,500 mg really is what you intend, tell me the clinical reason and I'll flag it in the order note for pharmacy review. I'd still advise against it."
      }
     ],
